# Fetching API Flow

- Pages should obtain data through dedicated hooks in `@/hooks`, not by calling services directly; this keeps UI concerns decoupled from networking logic.
- Hooks encapsulate state, side effects, and cache/mutation handling, and must delegate all HTTP requests to the appropriate module under `@/services`.
- Service modules are the single source of truth for API endpoints; they should perform request composition via shared clients (e.g., `@/lib/apiClient`) and expose typed helpers consumed by hooks.
- When introducing a new data workflow, follow the chain `page -> @/hooks -> @/services`, adding tests/mocks at the hook layer and keeping services free of React-specific logic.
